            </note>
            <note corresp="#d625-f2" n="19" xml:id="d625-f2-content">
                <p>
                    <ref target="frus1935v03#pg_786">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1935, Vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">iii</hi>, p. 786</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d625-f3" n="20" xml:id="d625-f3-content">
                <p>Not printed; in the final paragraph the Department instructed the Embassy that it
                    “should continue to oppose actively not only monopoly agreements which accord to
                    foreign interests an exclusive or preferential trade position but also
                    unreasonable restraints on international trade”. (893.602/45)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d625-f4" n="21" xml:id="d625-f4-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
